<p>TypeScript adds types to a language that already runs. Bayan starts with the types. If you use unions, narrowing and <code>strict</code> mode, much of this will look right: a value is a union of shapes, a <code>switch</code> narrows it, and <code>null</code> is only allowed where the type says so. The differences come from Bayan being compiled to a native program with no runtime: integers have sizes, memory has an owner, and a type that is wrong stops the build rather than being erased.</p>
<p>Every Bayan program on this page was run with the compiler, and the output shown is its real output.</p>

